  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05 (7 items, all closed).\n\nFrank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg: I first renewed it for 90 days + 1 refill. His most recent valid potassium was 4.5 on 1/20. The 5.9 from St. Brigid on 8/27 didn't count because the sample was hemolyzed, so I ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0002). While I was working, a new St. Brigid report arrived: BMP drawn 10/20 on a good sample, potassium 5.8. Under the protocol that means no refill, so I cancelled my renewal (nothing had been dispensed). He now has no active lisinopril prescription. I sent you an urgent task (task-t0017), sent him a corrected message with warning symptoms to watch for, and wrote a note. The repeat BMP order is still active. His hernia repair is set for 11/12.\n\nSamuel Price (pt-0030):\n- Metformin 1000 mg twice daily: his portal message and two pharmacy requests were one request. I placed one order (mr-t0006): 90 days + 1 refill. Basis: eGFR 58 (corrected from 65, still ≥45) and HbA1c 7.1% drawn 8/19 at an outside lab.\n- Lisinopril 20 mg: I first renewed it. The lab then corrected his 10/6 creatinine from 1.36 to 1.49. That is 35.5% above the 1.10 before his dose increase on 9/18, over the 30% limit, so the protocol treats it like a high potassium. I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0005). He has no active lisinopril and his 30-day supply has run out. I sent you an urgent task (task-t0018), sent him a corrected message and wrote a note.\n\nMarcus Webb (pt-0031):\n- Metformin 500 mg twice daily: renewed for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0013). The eGFR of 39 from 10/14 is marked entered in error and wasn't counted; his valid eGFR is 90–92 and his HbA1c 6.9% from 9/28.\n- Lisinopril 10 mg: at first his last BMP was too old (drawn 10/20/2025, just over 12 months), so I sent a 30-day supply with no refills and ordered a BMP. A BMP drawn 10/22 then came in with potassium 4.6, so I replaced the 30-day order with 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0019). I told him he doesn't need another draw for this refill. The BMP order I placed (sr-t0012) is no longer needed, and I had no way to cancel it, so please cancel it. I sent him a corrected message and wrote a note.\n\nMistakes in my records: when I closed Mr. Odum's message I didn't link my reply to him, though the reply was sent. Mr. Webb's 30-day lisinopril order shows as \"stopped\" (replaced) rather than cancelled.\n\nLeft open for you in the results queue: the three new results above (inbox-a0001, a0002, a0004). I acted on them but didn't close them. Other results are outside this request, and the protocol only lets me act for the patients who sent messages. Some need attention soon:\n- Critical potassium results: pt-0016 (6.3, open since 10/20) and pt-0008 (6.4, from 10/22).\n- An ED CT angiogram chest preliminary report for pt-0007.\n- Several other open results.",
